# Architectural integrity audit (new vs semantic-integrity-audit.md). Source: origin/main, read-only, nothing run.

| # | Area | Class |
|---|---|---|
| 1a | Import/layer/cycle checker (depcruise, madge, eslint boundaries, no-cycle) for Nexus's own cli/ | NOT PRESENT. git grep for those tool names finds only docs/PHASE4_IMPLEMENTATION_WORK_PACKAGES.md. No eslint/biome config in tree (only cli/tsconfig.json). CI (.github/workflows/ci.yml:58-92) runs sync-version, check_requirements, deprecated-lock, build, `git diff --exit-code cli/dist`, cargo test, `npm --prefix cli test`. Only cycle guards are data-level: operation.ts:536 (work-unit dependency cycle), task_message_log.ts:192 (message ancestry). core/tests/segregation_boundary.rs and cli/test/{credential_boundary,review_unit_boundary}.test.ts are security/role boundaries, not import layering. |
| 1b | Repo-level architecture rules the agent's change is checked against | NOT PRESENT. Acceptance consults tests/verifier only. The one path-scope check, eval/evaluators/code/diff_boundary.mjs:20-30 (allowedPaths), is an eval-task evaluator (used in cli/test/code_evaluators.test.ts:344,607,633), not wired to live-session acceptance. Classification: Missing. |
| 2 | Public-interface/schema/OpenAPI/persistence-format change detection and breaking-vs-compatible classification in a candidate diff | NOT PRESENT. grep for breaking change/public api/openapi/schema diff in cli/src and eval finds only: roles.ts:56 (prompt text "avoid unintended breaking changes"), specialist_profiles.ts:77 (a call-site-analysis escalation criterion string), worktrunk/ai_message.ts:60 (commit trailer). Advisory prose only. Nexus's OWN persisted formats are versioned: operation_schema.ts validateOperationState (:96), backupBeforeMigration refuses to overwrite a differing .pre-migration-vN copy (operation_runner_persistence.ts:~225), UnsupportedOperationSchemaError; tested by upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts. That protects Nexus state, not the target repo. Classification: Missing (target repo); Implemented+verified (own state schema). |
| 3 | Cross-operation / cumulative checks (architecture before/after, duplication, cumulative regression) | PARTIAL, narrow. Per-merge: operation_git.ts:388-420 merges each unit `--no-ff` into the integration worktree, re-runs that unit's verifier on the MERGED tree, and resets on failure (restoreIntegration :598); integrationIntegrity (:583) checks commit ancestry. This is cumulative in the sense that unit N is verified on top of units 1..N-1, but only with that unit's own verify command. No duplication, architecture-snapshot, or dependency-graph comparison anywhere. CERI baseline.ts/contracts.ts compare PASS/FAIL per eval definition (contracts.ts:145-146) across runs of Nexus itself, not across an agent session's successive edits to a repo. Classification: Partial for merge-time regression; Missing for architecture/duplication. |
| 4a | Single driver per operation | Implemented+verified-ish. operation_runner_persistence.ts:~185-215 `acquire()`: O_EXCL ("wx") lock file with pid/host/boot-time staleness takeover; OperationLockedError. Stale takeover is rmSync+create (small TOCTOU between two takeovers; not exploitable in single-user model, no finding asserted). |
| 4b | Durable state commits | Implemented. durable_file.ts:40,56,143-146,198,222 (temp + fsync + rename), state.ts:442-457 (dir fsync), state_restore.ts:132-136,237-249 (O_EXCL temp, O_NOFOLLOW, fsync, rename), task_message_log.ts:256-259 (fsync file+dir), config.ts:272-282, credentials.ts:181, ceri/evidence_store.ts:299-305 (rename, no fsync shown at that site). Corrupt state is quarantined by rename (state.ts:1132). Verification: compaction_crash_child.ts helper, upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts (11 crash refs), durable_continuity.test.ts (9). |
| 4c | Retry after unknown outcome | Implemented+verified. Inference timeout with possible execution -> kind "execution_unknown" (operation_runner_execution.ts:919) -> scheduler.ts:591-598 blocks unit with cause EXECUTION_UNKNOWN, "will not resubmit it elsewhere on its own", only operator "replay the step" re-runs. Branch already merged but result lost -> EXECUTION_UNKNOWN, restart-and-verify only (operation_runner.ts:385-395). Tests: operation_git.test.ts:750,882; team_convergence.test.ts:622; convergence_scheduling.test.ts:420. Scope: model-inference requests and integration; NOT a per-tool-call idempotency ledger. |
| 4d | Replay of interrupted unit | Partial / Implemented but inadequately verified for side effects. scheduler.ts:617-631 reconcileInterruptedRuns: a unit left RUNNING after a crash goes back to RUNNABLE and is re-run (unknownResumes++, blocks as INTERRUPTED only after policy.unknownResumeBudget). Its prior tool side effects in a NON-isolated operation are not rolled back or diffed; the agent re-reads state. In isolated mode the worktree is kept and "continues on the same files" (operation_git.ts:198) and merged-but-unrecorded units are recognised via merge-base --is-ancestor (:190,:346) so a crash between merge and persist does not merge twice. Test: operation_concurrency.test.ts:234 (MAO-07 restart reconciles in-flight units through real store). No test kills a process mid non-idempotent tool call. |
| 5 | Two units editing same region | Isolated mode (opt-in spec.git.isolate, operation.ts:277): DETECTED and BLOCKED. Per-unit worktree/branch (operation_git.ts:250); integration serialized by promise chain (operation_runner.ts:483-503); textual conflict -> merge --abort, branches kept, MERGE_CONFLICT decision for operator (operation_git.ts:392-396; operation_runner.ts:~506-512; test operation_git.test.ts:299-319). Semantic (non-textual) conflicts are caught only if the unit verifier fails on the merged tree. Non-isolated mode: default concurrency is 1 (operation_schema.ts:87-88, effectiveConcurrency), so no overlap by default; if the operator sets maxConcurrentUnits>1 without isolation, grep finds NO write-set/overlap check in scheduler.ts, operation.ts, operation_git.ts and no stale-write guard on edit tools (observation_identity.ts fileSignature is used for read-coverage dedupe, agent.ts:47, execution_tracking.ts, not to reject an edit based on a stale read). That is last-writer-wins by construction. Classification: Partial; I did not confirm via code trace that the schema forbids >1 without isolation, but found no such check (grep of maxConcurrentUnits: operation_schema.ts:88,126,170 only validate numeric range). |
| 6 | CERI scenarios and fault-injection tests | CERI domains (ceri/contracts.ts:3-18): code_comprehension, scoped_implementation, multi_file_refactoring, dependency_analysis, tool_selection, context_compaction, session_persistence, retry_backoff, rate_limit_recovery, model_escalation, specialist_delegation, independent_review, authorization_enforcement, workspace_isolation. No domain for architecture/dependency-rule preservation, contract breakage, concurrency/merge-conflict, or crash-during-side-effect; closest are multi_file_refactoring, dependency_analysis, workspace_isolation, session_persistence. CERI tests (ceri_*.test.ts: baseline, contracts, e2e, evidence_store, investigation, remediation, audit_findings) test the framework mechanics; grep finds no SIGKILL/crash scenario in ceri_*.test.ts. Real crash/concurrency tests live outside CERI: operation_concurrency.test.ts (14 tests, MAO-01..10, GIT-01/03/05), operation_git.test.ts, checkpoint_index_lock.test.ts, upgrade_transaction_recovery.test.ts, compaction_crash_child.ts, operation_release_acceptance/review tests (crash refs 22-23). Classification: Implemented but inadequately verified for the architecture/contract domains (no scenarios); crash/concurrency of the operation runtime is reasonably tested. |

## Summary classification
- Implemented+verified: unknown-outcome inference handling (EXECUTION_UNKNOWN), isolated-unit serialized merge with conflict block, durable atomic writes, single-driver lock, own state-schema versioning.
- Partial: merge-time per-unit re-verification (no cumulative architecture/duplication check); interrupted-unit replay in non-isolated ops (no side-effect ledger); same-region conflict (blocked only in isolated mode).
- Missing: import/layer/cycle enforcement for Nexus or target repo; contract/API/persistence-format diff classification for target repo; cross-operation architecture snapshot; CERI domains for architecture, contract, concurrency, fault injection.
- Defective: none confirmed. Caveat in 5 (unconfirmed concurrency>1 without isolation) is a gap-to-verify, not a defect.
